Table rows: a child that is not a cell goes in an anonymous cell

Not reported upstream from here (Postio does not contact upstream); as
of 0.3.0-beta.2 the table builder drops it.

Responsive mail stacks its columns on a narrow screen by making its
layout-table cells `display: block; width: 100%` under
`@media (max-width: 600px)`. A `display: block` child of a row is not a
table-cell, and `collect_table_cells` sent it to the arm for captions,
which removes its construction damage and leaves it out of the table's
layout children: never laid out, never painted, text and images gone.
CSS 2.1 §17.2.1 wraps each run of consecutive non-cell children of a row
(block or inline level, not captions or other internal table boxes) in
one anonymous table-cell; the run stacks inside it as blocks, the way
browsers draw these newsletters. The anonymous cell is the anonymous
block `construct.rs` already makes (now `create_anonymous_box`), styled
from the row, placed like a one-column cell, and owned by the table so
the next construction deallocates it.

Tested by crates/postio-render/tests/engine_patches.rs and, on a
corpus newsletter in the app-colours column, tests/treatment.rs.

